# Line endings.
#
# The repository already stores LF everywhere. What this file fixes is the
# working tree: with core.autocrlf=true (the Git for Windows default) a
# checkout rewrites text files to CRLF, and two things then break on Windows
# that are fine on Linux and in CI.
#
# 1. `scripts/generate-editorial-drafts.mjs --check` regenerates a fixture in
#    memory with LF and compares it byte-for-byte against the file on disk.
#    A CRLF checkout can never match, so `pnpm test` fails on Windows with a
#    "stale fixture" error that has nothing to do with the fixture.
#
# 2. Shell scripts under ops/ run inside Linux containers. They are mounted
#    from the working tree by docker-compose, not copied from the repo, so a
#    CRLF checkout is what the container actually executes -- and a script
#    whose shebang ends in \r fails with "bad interpreter".
#
# Declaring the endings here makes them a property of the repository rather
# than of each contributor's git config.

# Normalise to LF in the repository; let the platform decide the checkout for
# anything not pinned below.
* text=auto

# Executed on Linux -- must be LF in the working tree on every platform.
*.sh text eol=lf
ops/** text eol=lf

# Compared byte-for-byte against generator output, which emits LF.
apps/api/src/seed-data/*.json text eol=lf

# Generated and read by tooling that assumes LF.
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.cjs text eol=lf

# Never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.sqlite binary
*.exe binary
